---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { SignalDefenderGame } from '../../components/Games/games'

const title = 'Signal Defender — A Morse Code Listening Game | MorseForge'
const description =
  'Characters fall and sound as they appear. Type each one before it reaches the floor. A Morse code game about copying at speed, not about knowing the alphabet.'
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/games/signal-defender/">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-14">
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Signal Defender</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Characters fall, one sounding as each appears. Type it before it lands.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <SignalDefenderGame client:load />
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-10">
      <h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">What a game is for</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Not learning. Practice teaches, and it waits for you — you can sit on a character for ten
        seconds and still be told you were right. That is correct for learning and useless as a
        measure, because copying at speed does not fail on characters you cannot decode. It fails on
        characters you cannot decode <em>before the next one arrives</em>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        This is that gap, made visible. Everything you knock down still feeds the same review
        schedule as practice, so a run is not thrown away — but what it is really for is the list at
        the end of what got past you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-8 font-display text-xl font-bold tracking-tight">It plays with sound off</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Each falling signal shows its dots and dashes as well as its letter, so with sound off in
        <a href="/settings/" class="text-signal underline underline-offset-4">settings</a> this becomes
        a reading game instead of a listening one. Slower to get hard, and still worth playing.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The other one is <a
          href="/games/morse-runner/"
          class="text-signal underline underline-offset-4">Morse Runner</a
        >, which is the same idea for sending.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
